  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_019, acc=0.639) uses PCA as the RNA encoder in a multimodal, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted-fusion setup. RNA-only experiments show that multi-profile + avgpool is strongly preferred over single-profile or transformer (0.591 vs 0.485/0.519), and weighted fusion edges out concat (0.639 vs 0.619). However, the RNA encoder has only been tested as PCA—a simple linear projection. Image-only performance is very low (0.208), indicating RNA carries the dominant signal, so the quality of the RNA representation is likely the highest-leverage remaining design choice. Question tested: Does a learned nonlinear RNA encoder (scvi_n200) improve over PCA in the best multimodal configuration? This is a single-variable swap from config_019, making the result clean and directly interpretable. Why this is the best next experiment: If scvi_n200 improves performance, it confirms that RNA representation quality is a bottleneck and justifies further investment in learned encoders (scgpt, etc.). If it does not, PCA is confirmed as sufficient and the search can focus on other axes (e.g., image encoder). Either outcome sharply reduces uncertainty about the most important remaining design decision, making this the most information-efficient use of the next budget slot."
}

